@*
    Forgotten password (Task 1 8.2). The client has no email service, so there is
    no reset link. The Managing Director issues a new temporary password from the
    Users screen, and the user chooses their own at the next sign-in. This page
    says so; it collects nothing and sends nothing.
*@
@{
    Layout = "_AuthLayout";
    ViewData["Title"] = "Forgotten password";
}

<a class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm auth-back" asp-action="Login">
    <svg class="ico ico-sm" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow-left" /></svg> Back to sign in
</a>

<h1>Forgotten your password?</h1>
<p class="lede">
    Ask the Managing Director for a new temporary password. Passwords are not reset by email,
    because the system does not send email.
</p>

<ol class="auth-steps">
    <li>The Managing Director opens <strong>Users</strong> and chooses <strong>New password</strong> next to your name.</li>
    <li>They give you the temporary password in person. It is shown to them only once.</li>
    <li>Sign in with your email address and the temporary password.</li>
    <li>Choose your own password straight away. Until you do, no other page opens.</li>
</ol>

<div class="notice notice-info" role="note">
    <svg class="ico" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-info" /></svg>
    <div>
        <strong>Locked out after too many attempts?</strong>
        A new temporary password from the Managing Director also unlocks the account.
    </div>
</div>

<a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg btn-block auth-action" asp-action="Login">Back to sign in</a>
